<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Troia, Apulia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Troia is a hill town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, founded around 1019 by the Byzantine catepan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basil-boioannes">Basil Boioannes</a> as a fortress guarding the frontier against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> principalities. It soon became a bishopric. Its Romanesque cathedral, with a rose window and bronze doors of the 12th century, is one of the finest in Apulia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/troia-apulia.jpg" alt="Troia, Apulia" width="320" height="291" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tango7174 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Troia_(FG)_-_duomo_-_vista_notturna.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
